<title>GERMANY: TABLE - W.German May industry orders fall 1.1pct m/m.</title>
<headline>TABLE - W.German May industry orders fall 1.1pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     May 97   April 97	May 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -1.1	 +3.7	  -0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+5.5	 +6.3	  -2.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		100.3	101.4	  95.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   May 97 April 97   May 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders		-0.8     +3.3	89.3</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 -1.4     +4.1     122.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +0.6     +2.4     103.8</p>
<p> Capital goods		  -1.8     +4.6     101.1</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   -3.9     +5.5	90.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Apr/May 97 with Feb/Mar 97:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +3.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr/May 97 with Apr/May 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +6.3</p>
<p> Domestic orders			+3.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			+11.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +8.9</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +4.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +3.1</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
